+### Optimized TensorRT Result
+
+GR00T N1.7 Inference Timing, measured under the following setup:
+
+-  **AGX Thor**:  MAXN power mode, **JetPack 7.2**
+- **Engine build:** `--execution-profile optimized` with `--quantization fp8` or
+  `mixed_nvfp4` (see [Performance Optimization](#performance-optimization))
+
+| Device | Dataset | Configuration | Data Processing | Backbone | Action Head | E2E | Frequency | E2E Speedup |
+|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+|  AGX Thor | LIBERO | PyTorch Eager | 8.21 ms | 55.26 ms | 81.65 ms | 144.9 ms | 6.9 Hz | 1.00x |
+|  AGX Thor | LIBERO | TensorRT Full Pipeline | 8.21 ms | 28.89 ms | 56.64 ms | 93.8 ms | 10.7 Hz | 1.54x |
+|  AGX Thor | LIBERO | **TensorRT Full Pipeline Optimized + FP8** | 8.21 ms | 14.04 ms | 20.69 ms | **42.9 ms** | **23.3 Hz** | **3.37x** |
+|  AGX Thor | LIBERO | **TensorRT Full Pipeline Optimized + mixed NVFP4** | 8.21 ms | 13.53 ms | 17.22 ms | **38.9 ms** | **25.7 Hz** | **3.73x** |
+
+Optimized mixed NVFP4 is 2.41x faster than the standard TensorRT full pipeline
+(93.8 ms → 38.9 ms E2E) with no measurable accuracy loss: averaged over 3 rounds of
+the 200-episode LIBERO Spatial closed-loop benchmark on Thor, it reaches 97.3%
+success vs. 97.5% for the PyTorch bf16 baselines.
+
